Constraints:
- Licensing limitations
- Storage costs
- Must not reduce premium value

Trade-offs:
- Limit number of discovery downloads per user
- Time-bound access
- A song can be downloaded for only 7 continuous days per user
- Feature restricted to emerging artists only

Out of Scope:
- Permanent offline access for free users
- Revenue or licensing model changes
- Full catalog downloads


Definition:
Constraints: Fixed limitations or conditions that restrict how a solution can be designed or implemented.
Trade-offs: Deliberate decisions where improving one aspect of a solution requires compromising another, in order to best meet business and technical goals.
